  "decision": "The highest observed clean single-request BF16-KV completion is 53,248 total context tokens when the contiguous KV pool is pre-sized to 208 pages. That row has only 0.025013 GiB sampled headroom and is a physical-roof diagnostic, not a reliable operating point. The next 1K boundary, 54,272 tokens with 212 pre-sized pages, aborts with HSA_STATUS_ERROR_OUT_OF_RESOURCES; 54K, 56K, 63K, and 64K corroborate the upper failure. Keep 32,768 as the supported operational setting because its real request retains 2.114937 GiB headroom. The default 128-page lazy pool also crosses a duplicate-backing cliff above 32K: 33,024 succeeds with only 0.030937 GiB headroom after allocating a second contiguous chunk.",
